Field contract: supporting_evidence contains the exact supplied claim, participant, and review IDs. Put every declared participant ID in the supporting_evidence of its person subject exactly once. alternate_names contains only alternate human names explicitly written in the source; evidence IDs are not names.

Participant IDs identify the named speakers themselves. They do not identify the subjects of everything those speakers say. Include each speaker as a person even when none of the claims describe that speaker. A speaker who reports another person's action and that other person are separate subjects. Assign the participant ID only to the speaker's subject; cite claim IDs for the people described by those claims.
